[
  {
    "comment": "Chorong's default keymap, in Zed's keymap format: sections of context + keystroke -> action. `cmd` means Cmd on macOS and Ctrl elsewhere (the loader rewrites it); a section tagged \"platform\" applies to that platform only. See docs/public/keybindings.md.",
    "context": "Chorong",
    "bindings": {
      "cmd-p": "chorong::OpenPicker",
      "cmd-shift-p": "chorong::OpenPalette",
      "cmd-o": "chorong::OpenPath",
      "cmd-shift-o": "chorong::OpenSymbols",
      "cmd-t": "chorong::OpenProjectSymbols",
      "cmd-f": "chorong::FindInFile",
      "cmd-shift-f": "chorong::OpenSearch",
      "ctrl-g": "chorong::GoToLine",
      "f12": "chorong::GoToDefinition",
      "shift-f12": "chorong::FindReferences",
      "cmd-[": "chorong::Back",
      "cmd-]": "chorong::Forward",
      "ctrl--": "chorong::Back",
      "ctrl-shift--": "chorong::Forward",
      "cmd-k l": "chorong::ToggleCriticalLens",
      "cmd-k h": "chorong::ToggleHideTests",
      "cmd-k o": "chorong::ToggleOutline",
      "cmd-k shift-h": "chorong::ToggleHighlights",
      "cmd-k b": "chorong::ToggleFileTree",
      "cmd-k shift-b": "chorong::ToggleBlame",
      "cmd-k p": "chorong::TogglePin",
      "cmd-k g": "chorong::ShowGraph",
      "cmd-k i": "chorong::BuildIndex",
      "cmd-k e": "chorong::OpenInEditor",
      "cmd-k w": "chorong::OpenOnGitHub",
      "cmd-k c": "chorong::CopyLink",
      "cmd-k d": "chorong::CompareAgainst",
      "cmd-k u": "chorong::ToggleHighlightUncommitted",
      "cmd-k t": "chorong::SwitchTheme",
      "cmd-k 0": "chorong::FoldAll",
      "cmd-k j": "chorong::UnfoldAll"
    }
  },
  {
    "context": "Chorong",
    "platform": "other",
    "bindings": {
      "alt-left": "chorong::Back",
      "alt-right": "chorong::Forward"
    }
  },
  {
    "comment": "Second keys for the pickers on macOS, as some Zed keymaps bind them (Cmd-T and Cmd-P keep working).",
    "context": "Chorong",
    "platform": "macos",
    "bindings": {
      "cmd-n": "chorong::OpenProjectSymbols",
      "ctrl-cmd-n": "chorong::OpenPicker"
    }
  },
  {
    "comment": "The macOS menu bar's Quit and Minimize. No context: they work in every Chorong window, the settings window too.",
    "platform": "macos",
    "bindings": {
      "cmd-q": "chorong::Quit",
      "cmd-m": "chorong::MinimizeWindow"
    }
  },
  {
    "comment": "Settings window. No context: the key also works inside the settings window itself.",
    "bindings": {
      "cmd-,": "chorong::OpenSettings"
    }
  },
  {
    "comment": "Layout actions (docks, panes, focus layouts). Keys follow the layout design. MinimizePane, ReopenFocusLayout and the dock toggles have no key there except those below, so the rest stay reachable from the pane menu, the status bar and the focus-history button. The viewer's own binding wins where a key is taken: Cmd-K P stays Toggle pin, and Esc (RestoreLayout) is not bound here because the code view's Esc clears highlights, which hands over to the layout when a menu or focus layout is open.",
    "context": "Chorong",
    "bindings": {
      "cmd-k m": "chorong::ToggleMaximizePane",
      "cmd-k shift-p": "chorong::PinContextToBottomBar",
      "cmd-k f": "chorong::ToggleFrameStats"
    }
  },
  {
    "comment": "Pins and tour pages (design/layout.md). Cmd-K P (Toggle pin, above) pins the context under the live Context pane, or unpins a focused pin; Cmd-K Shift-P pins to the bottom bar. Cmd-K R rebuilds the current focus page from the tour step that made it.",
    "context": "Chorong",
    "bindings": {
      "cmd-k r": "chorong::ResetFocusPage"
    }
  },
